=== 6. did fusing the IMU help? =======================================
                               position [m]    heading [deg]
  wheel odometry alone               5.2420           8.8536
  EKF, wheels + gyro                 3.2993         -12.9539

  WHY, MEASURED RATHER THAN ASSERTED:
  mean gyro z over the run     -0.001205 rad/s  (12100 samples)
  the vehicle's own mean yaw rate  +0.001404 rad/s (ground truth)
  the difference, the BIAS     -0.002610 rad/s  (model.sdf declares 0.002618, sign drawn by gz)
  bias x duration              -0.3156 rad = -18.08 deg
  EKF heading error            -0.2261 rad = -12.95 deg
  The filter is tracking the gyro. The IMU arrives at 100 Hz and the
  wheel odometry at 50 Hz, so the gyro gets twice the corrections, and
  the package-default process noise on yaw rate is large enough that
  the estimate follows whichever measurement came last. The message
  covariance the filter is given carries the gyro's WHITE NOISE only.
  [note] this comparison is REPORTED, not required to come out either way. A gyro whose bias the filter is not told about can make heading worse, and that is a finding about cheap MEMS IMUs rather than a defect.

=== 6b. the same run, split into moving and standing ==================
  THE SPLIT IS TAKEN FROM THE VEHICLE'S OWN ENCODER
  VERDICT, not from the profile's nominal timings and
  not from ground truth. Its purpose is to show which
  part of the run a change to standstill handling can
  possibly have touched.

  recorded window            120.98 s
  of which the wheels were
    reported standing still  10.20 s
  first / last moving sample 26.12 s .. 136.88 s
  gyro samples on /forklift/imu 12100
  gyro samples on /forklift/imu_gated 11077   (zero means the gate is
    not running and the filter is remapped onto the raw topic, not that it lost its gyro)

  heading error at the first moving sample  -0.0598 deg
  heading error at the last moving sample   -12.9539 deg
  DRIFT ACCUMULATED WHILE MOVING            -12.8941 deg over 110.76 s
  bias x MOVING seconds                     -16.5602 deg
  bias x RECORDED seconds                   -18.0838 deg
  [note] the moving-only figure is the one to compare across builds. A change that only affects standing intervals leaves it alone and shortens the whole-run figure by bias x the standing seconds; a change that also flatters the moving case moves it, and would be doing something other than what it claims.

=== 7. the drift against what it has to exercise ======================
  sim/worlds/WAREHOUSE_LANDMARKS.md section 5 names three
  degenerate stretches, 4.0 to 5.5 m long, in which the scan
  carries almost no along-aisle information and odometry has
  to carry the vehicle across them.

  measured position error      3.2993 m over 106.49 m
  pro rata over the longest
  degenerate stretch, 5.5 m    0.1704 m
  [note] the pro-rata figure is an ORDER OF MAGNITUDE and not a prediction: dead-reckoning error grows with heading error, so it is superlinear in distance and depends on the manoeuvres, not only on how far the vehicle went

